{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And these are the judgments.</b> Rashi's comment: every place where 'these' is said disqualifies the preceding ones, that is, these and not the preceding ones. And do not object to me with 'these are the commandments' in the portion of Bechukotai and in the portion of Masei, 'these are the statutes' in the portion of Matot, 'these are the words of the covenant' in the portion of Ki Tavo, and similar cases, for there it is not appropriate to interpret them thus, because there the matter concludes [the topic]. And as for 'and these are the judgments' — Rabbi Abbahu said, Rabbi Yossi ben Zimra said: every place where 'these' is said disqualifies the preceding ones, while 'and these' adds to the preceding ones, as it is written: 'there He made for him a statute and a judgment.' <b>The judgments.</b> Above, He instructed them in the order of their reverence; from here onward, He instructs them in the order of laws. Another interpretation: above He wrote the warnings — 'You shall not murder,' 'You shall not commit adultery,' etc. — and did not specify the punishments if a person transgresses them. He returned and specified what their punishment is. What Rashi explained here — why was the portion of laws juxtaposed to the portion of the altar — teaches us that this is not the [natural] place of the portion of laws, for if you examine the matter well, reason dictates that the entire portion, from 'When you buy' until 'Six years you shall sow,' is included in the portion of Behar. And on this Rashi commented: 'and these' adds to the preceding ones — that is, to the laws written in the portion of Behar." "<b>Before them.</b> Rashi's comment: and not before Canaanites, even if they are experts. But if Israelites judged him first and he did not comply with the ruling, it is permitted to coerce him by means of Canaanites until he does what the Israelite judges ruled upon him."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:12.467697154Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}